The ring will have one record with attrs [id=abc, user=bob]. The "req" group is lost. This might be fine for tests that just check records are stored.

But if a test expects groups to be preserved... Let me think. The slog.Record doesn't have a "group" attribute. Groups are reflected in the attr names (e.g., "req.id", "req.user") in text/json handlers. For a record stored in memory, the attrs are just flat - there's no inherent "group" nesting.

Given that the spec doesn't mention groups or WithAttrs/WithGroup behavior at all, I think a simple implementation is fine. Let me just make it work correctly for the basic cases.

